course: dictionary
lesson: 1104
title: One word, many branches
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Branch has more than one meaning, so the words around it tell you which one you need. «The potoo sits still on a branch looking exactly like a dead stump.» The sitting still and the stump point to a tree, so here a branch is a part of a tree.
explain: The same word can name a shop or office too. A bank with a branch in your town has an office there that belongs to the same bank. In a maths tree diagram, the branches show choices. Each time, ask: which meaning fits the sentence?
explain: Branch can also be a verb. To branch out means to split into parts or to start doing new things. Test your meaning by putting it into the sentence in place of the hard word. If it still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
fact: Branch can be a noun (a branch, branches) or a verb (to branch, branching).
fact: A branch is a part of a tree that grows out from the trunk and holds leaves up to the sunlight.
fact: A branch can also be one of the shops or offices of a company, like a branch of a bank.
fact: To branch out means to split into parts or start doing new things.
fact: When climbing, test each branch before you trust it, and stay off dead, dry or cracked branches, which can snap.
exercise: «The potoo sits still on a branch looking exactly like a dead stump.» What is a branch in this sentence? | A river that splits off | A shop in a town | A bank office | *A part of a tree that grows out from the trunk
exercise: Ryan says a branch of the bank opened near his house. What does branch mean here? | A dead stump | A part of a tree | *One of the offices that belong to the same bank | To split into parts
exercise: Which phrase means to split into parts or start doing new things? | To climb up | To trust | *To branch out | To snap off
test: «Red pandas wrap their thick tail around themselves like a blanket and have fur on the soles of their feet for icy branches.» In this sentence, branches are | Choices in a maths diagram | Shops that sell blankets | Parts of a river | *Parts of trees that the pandas walk on
test: In a maths tree diagram, the branches show | *Choices | Sunlight | Roots | Leaves
exam: In «an if picks only one branch each run», branch means | Dead wood on the ground | *One of the choices the code can take | A bank office | A part of a tree's trunk
